---
const { product } = Astro.props;
const zipper = product.slug === 'zipper-bags';
const bubble = product.slug === 'poly-bubble-mailers';
---
<details class="size-comparison" id="size-comparison" data-size-comparison hidden>
  <summary>Need a starting model? Compare your packed item with catalogue sizes</summary>
  <div class="comparison-content">
    <h3>Compare {product.name} Outer Sizes</h3>
    <p>Measure the complete pack, including wrapping and inserts. This tool shortlists catalogue sizes for review; confirm usable inner space and test a filled sample before ordering.</p>
    <form data-size-form class="size-form">
      <div class="size-fields">
        <div><label for="packed-unit">Measurement unit</label><select id="packed-unit" name="unit"><option value="cm">Centimeters (cm)</option><option value="in">Inches (in)</option></select></div>
        <div><label for="packed-width">Packed width</label><input id="packed-width" name="width" type="number" min="0.001" max="1000" step="any" required inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 24" /></div>
        <div><label for="packed-length">Packed length</label><input id="packed-length" name="length" type="number" min="0.001" max="1000" step="any" required inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 30" /></div>
        <div><label for="packed-thickness">Packed thickness</label><input id="packed-thickness" name="thickness" type="number" min="0.001" max="1000" step="any" required inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 4" /><small>Depth of the complete pack, not film gauge.</small></div>
        <div><label for="packed-allowance">Extra allowance per flat dimension</label><input id="packed-allowance" name="allowance" type="number" min="0" max="20" step="any" value="2" required inputmode="decimal" /><small>Starts at 2 cm (about 0.79 in). Adjust this comparison assumption; it is not a verified fit allowance or production tolerance.</small></div>
      </div>
      <button class="button button-secondary" type="submit">Compare Catalogue Sizes</button>
    </form>
    <p class="comparison-status" data-size-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div data-size-results hidden>
      <p class="comparison-reference" data-size-reference></p>
      <div class="size-candidates" data-size-candidates></div>
      <p data-size-limits>{zipper ? 'Catalogue height is an outer reference. Confirm the usable height below the zipper and the clear opening.' : bubble ? 'The bubble liner, seams and opening reduce usable space. Their dimensions are not deducted by this tool.' : 'Confirm usable inner dimensions, seam allowances and flap closure on the actual bag.'}</p>
      <button class="text-link manual-size" type="button" data-size-help>Add measurements to my brief and ask for sizing help →</button>
      <p class="comparison-application" data-size-application role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="#brief-selection-form">Review or edit your quote brief ↓</a></p>
    </div>
    <details class="comparison-method"><summary>How the outer-size comparison works</summary><p>For this screening reference, we add the full packed thickness and your extra allowance to each packed flat dimension: width + thickness + allowance, and length + thickness + allowance. We also check a 90° rotation of packed width and length. Thickness stays the same.</p><p>{zipper ? 'The reference is compared with catalogue outer width and height, not a confirmed measurement below the zipper.' : 'The reference is compared with catalogue outer width and body length. The “+ flap” is excluded from body length.'} Candidates are ordered by outer width × body length{zipper ? ' / height' : ''}, smallest area first. This ranking does not establish usable capacity, availability or protection.</p><p>The starting allowance is adjustable. Lining, seals, tolerances, irregular shapes and insertion can change the size needed. If no candidate is listed, ask us to review your measurements and custom options.</p></details>
  </div>
</details>
<style>
  .size-comparison{scroll-margin-top:100px;margin:0 0 28px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:#fff;min-width:0}.size-comparison[hidden],.size-comparison [hidden]{display:none}.size-comparison>summary{cursor:pointer;padding:20px 24px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.6}.comparison-content{padding:0 24px 24px;min-width:0}.comparison-content h3{font-size:1.4rem;margin:0 0 12px}.comparison-content p{font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.7}.size-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin:22px 0}.size-fields>div{min-width:0}.size-fields label{display:block;font-size:.87rem;font-weight:650;margin-bottom:8px}.size-fields input,.size-fields select{box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:11px 12px;font:inherit;font-size:16px;background:#fff;color:var(--ink)}.size-fields small{display:block;font-size:.76rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5;margin-top:7px}.comparison-status:empty,.comparison-application:empty{display:none}.comparison-status,.comparison-application{font-weight:650}.comparison-reference{padding:16px;background:var(--cream);border-radius:8px}.size-candidates{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;margin:18px 0}.size-candidates :global(article){min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:18px}.size-candidates :global(h4){font-size:1.1rem;margin:0 0 8px}.size-candidates :global(p){margin:8px 0;font-size:.86rem;line-height:1.6}.size-candidates :global(button){white-space:normal;width:100%;margin-top:10px;justify-content:center;font-size:.85rem}.manual-size{background:none;border:0;padding:0;font:inherit;font-size:.9rem;cursor:pointer;text-align:left}.comparison-method{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:16px;margin-top:22px}.comparison-method summary{font-size:.9rem;font-weight:650;cursor:pointer}.comparison-content .button{white-space:normal}.comparison-content{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:760px){.size-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.size-candidates{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:440px){.size-fields{grid-template-columns:1fr}.size-comparison>summary{padding:18px 16px}.comparison-content{padding:0 16px 20px}}
</style>
